6.06.01. RR Rural Residential District.
(1) Purpose and intent. The Rural Residential District is comprised primarily of limited agricultural activities in areas where single-family residential development has occurred or is occurring. The regulations for this DISTRICT are designed to provide the landowner an opportunity to engage in limited hobby type agricultural activities for personal use, with the exception of fresh fruits, flowers or vegetables grown on the property which may be sold to the public, provided this exception does not extend to allow the operation of a commercial greenhouse or nursery. The DISTRICT is designed to encourage single-family development in a rural setting and certain uses allied to or customarily incidental to residential developments in a rural area.
(2) PRINCIPAL USE and STRUCTURES. PRINCIPAL USES and STRUCTURES shall be allowed in the RR Rural Residential District in accordance with section 6.04.01.
(3) ACCESSORY USE and STRUCTURES. ACCESSORY USES and STRUCTURES shall be permitted in the RR Rural Residential District in accordance with sections 5.05 and 6.04.01.
(4) CONDITIONAL USE. Conditional uses shall be permitted in the RR Rural Residential DISTRICT in accordance with section 6.04.01.
6.06.02. R-1 Single-Family Residential.
(1) Purpose and intent. The R-1 Single-Family Residential District is composed of low DENSITY single-family residential development. The DISTRICT is designed to encourage single-family development in a rural setting and certain uses allied to or customarily incidental to residential DEVELOPMENTS in a rural area.
(2) PRINCIPAL USE and STRUCTURES. PRINCIPAL USES and STRUCTURES shall be allowed in the R-1 Single-family Residential District in accordance with section 6.04.01.
(3) ACCESSORY USE and STRUCTURES. Accessory uses and STRUCTURES shall be permitted in the R-1 Single-Family Residential District in accordance with sections 5.05 and 6.04.01.
(4) CONDITIONAL USE. Conditional uses shall be permitted in the R-1 Single-family Residential District in accordance with section 6.04.01.
6.06.03. R-2 Single-Family and Two-Family Residential District.
(1) Purpose and Intent. The R-2 Single-Family Residential District is mainly comprised of single-family and two-family development, including SINGLE-FAMILY DWELLINGS, and manufactured housing, where surrounding land uses are compatible with DENSITY greater than minimum densities permitted in the R-1 district and where such development would not have an adverse impact on the surrounding areas.
(2) PRINCIPAL USE and STRUCTURES. PRINCIPAL USES and STRUCTURES shall be allowed in the R-2 Single-Family and Two-Family Residential District in accordance with section 6.04.01.
(3) ACCESSORY USE and STRUCTURES. ACCESSORY USES and STRUCTURES shall be permitted in the R-2 Single-family and Two-Family Residential District in accordance with sections 5.05 and 6.04.01.
(4) CONDITIONAL USE. Conditional uses shall be permitted in the R-2 Single-Family and Two-Family Residential District in accordance with section 6.04.01.
6.06.03A. R-2 Multi-Family Residential Standards.
1. (a) Multiple DUPLEXES, being more than one DWELLING, TWO FAMILY, as defined in section 3.01;
(b) Quadplexes, being four residential DWELLING UNITS combined into one building;
(c) Triplexes, being three individual DWELLING UNITS combined into one building; and
(d) TOWNHOUSES as defined in section 3.01 are PERMITTED USES in R-2 districts if they meet the following criteria:
(i) Development and/or rezoning for construction of multiple duplexes, triplexes, quadplexes, and townhouses calling for 20 or more units shall be fully fenced in with a minimum eight-foot-tall fence not to exceed 12 feet, and an operational gate which limits access of the general public and shall meet the requirements of section 66-55 of this appendix. The fence and gate shall be well maintained and meet the visual aesthetics of the units. No wire or chain-link fence will be allowed. All fencing must be approved by the planning and zoning office and may require a separate permit.
(ii) The DEVELOPMENT shall preserve 15 percent of its property as green space;
(iii) The height of the units shall not exceed two stories;
(iv) The minimum square footage of each unit shall be 950 square feet of heated floor space;
(v) The minimum SETBACKS shall be 20 feet from front road RIGHT-OF-WAY and 20 feet from all sides of property line;
(vi) The exterior of units shall be constructed of brick, rock, man-made rock, or cement board;
(vii) Carports if any shall be to the side or rear of the units;
(viii) Each unit shall have a minimum of three parking spaces with paved driveway, asphalt or concrete, and guttered and be well maintained;
(ix) All outdoor lighting shall be pointed in a downward direction;
(x) Accessory STRUCTURES shall be for use by residents only, and may only consist of laundry BUILDINGS, water and sewer BUILDINGS, fitness centers, indoor swimming POOLS, park and playground BUILDINGS, and clubhouses/common use BUILDINGS. The minimum square footage of fitness centers shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of indoor swimming pool BUILDINGS shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of park and playground BUILDINGS shall be 500 square feet. The minimum square footage of clubhouses/common use buildings shall be 1,200 square feet. Accessory STRUCTURES shall not occupy more than ten percent of total acreage;
(xi) HOME OCCUPATION businesses shall not be located in a unit unless the specific business at that specific location is approved by the PLANNING COMMISSION and BOARD of COMMISSIONERS upon proper application;
(xii) A one-hour firewall shall be constructed between each unit;
(xiii) Each unit shall have installed operational sprinklers approved and inspected by a certified third party and inspected on a routine basis to ensure proper operation; and
(xiv) An approved leak-proof container with close-fitting covers for the storage of garbage shall be on site. The container shall be emptied in a timely manner as to not let garbage overflow or fall onto the ground. The garbage facilities shall be adequately screened so they are not visible from the units, any STREETS, or any adjoining properties, and shall meet the SETBACKS of this section.
2. Apartments defined as DWELLING, MULTI-FAMILY, in section 3.01 and CONDOMINIUMS as defined in section 3.01 are PERMITTED USES in R-2 districts if they meet the following criteria:
(i) The constructions of a DEVELOPMENT of apartments and CONDOMINIUMS with 20 or more units shall be fully fenced in with a minimum eight-foot-tall fence not to exceed 12 feet and an operational gate which limits access of the general public and shall meet the requirements of section 66-55 of this appendix. The fence and gate shall be well maintained and meet the visual aesthetics of the units. No wire or chain-link fence will be allowed. All fencing must be approved by the planning and zoning office and may require a separate permit;
(ii) The DEVELOPMENT shall preserve 15 percent of its total acreage of property as green space to be subtracted from the total acreage when determining maximum DENSITY;
(iii) The minimum SETBACKS shall be 20 feet from front road RIGHT-OF-WAY and 20 feet from all sides of property line;
(iv) The units shall have approved septic and water systems;
(v) The height of the units shall not exceed three stories;
(vi) The minimum square footage of each unit shall be 650 square feet of heated floor space;
(vii) The exterior of units shall be constructed of brick, rock, man-made rock, or cement board;
(viii) All BUILDINGS shall have gutters on roof and downspouts:
(ix) Apartments and CONDOMINIUMS must have sidewalks at the fronts of all BUILDINGS with a minimum of five feet between each BUILDING and sidewalk for grass and shrubs/plants;
(x) Parking lots and streets/driveways shall be paved, curbed and guttered, and shall be well maintained;
(xi) The DEVELOPMENT shall have two ingress and two egress points which shall be paved, asphalt or concrete, for the first 75 units. In the event the number of units in the DEVELOPMENT exceed 75 units, the following shall apply:
• For 76 units to 150 units: one additional ingress/egress point shall be required;
• For 151 units to 225 units: two additional ingress/egress points shall be required;
• The above equation shall apply up to the full allowable capacity of the DEVELOPMENT;
(xii) The DEVELOPMENT shall front on a COUNTY or state paved roadway;
(xiii) The DEVELOPMENT shall have a minimum of three parking spaces per unit plus one additional parking space for each reasonably anticipated employee;
(xiv) All outdoor lighting shall be pointed in a downward direction;
(xv) Accessory STRUCTURES shall be for use by residents only, and may only consist of laundry BUILDINGS, water and sewer BUILDINGS, fitness centers, indoor swimming pools, park and playground BUILDINGS, and clubhouses/common use buildings. The minimum square footage of fitness centers shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of indoor swimming pool BUILDINGS shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of park and playground BUILDINGS shall be 500 square feet. The minimum square footage of clubhouses/common use buildings shall be 1,200 square feet. Accessory STRUCTURES shall not occupy more than ten percent of total acreage;
(xvi) A one-hour firewall shall be constructed between each unit;
(xvii) Each unit shall have installed operational sprinklers approved and inspected by a certified third party and inspected on a routine basis to ensure proper operation; and
(xviii) An approved leak-proof container with close-fitting covers for the storage of garbage shall be on site. The container shall be emptied in a timely manner as to not let garbage overflow or fall onto the ground. The garbage facilities shall be adequately screened so they are not visible from the units, any STREETS, or any adjoining properties, and shall meet the SETBACKS of this section.
3. ASSISTED LIVING facility (ASSISTED LIVING is a type of housing designed for people who need various levels of medical and personal care. The facilities generally provide a home-like setting and are physically designed to promote the resident's independence). ASSISTED LIVING facilities are PERMITTED USES in R-2 districts if they meet the following criteria:
(i) The construction of a DEVELOPMENT of ASSISTED LIVING facilities with 20 or more units shall be fully fenced in with an eight-foot-tall fence not to exceed 12 feet and an operational gate which limits access of the general public and shall meet the requirements of section 66-55 of this appendix. The fence and gate shall be well maintained and meet the visual aesthetics of the units, No wire or chain-link fence will be allowed. All fencing must be approved by the planning and zoning office and may require a separate permit;
(ii) The DEVELOPMENT shall preserve 15 percent of its property as green space;
(iii) The minimum SETBACKS shall be 20 feet from front road RIGHT-OF-WAY and 20 feet from all sides of property line;
(iv) The DEVELOPMENT shall have one and one-half; parking spaces per resident in the facility plus one additional parking space for each reasonably anticipated employee of the facility;
(v) Parking lots and streets/driveways shall be paved, curbed and guttered, and shall be well maintained;
(vi) The facility must have sidewalks at the fronts of all BUILDINGS with a minimum of five feet between each BUILDING and sidewalk for grass and shrubs/plants;
(vii) The height of the facility shall not exceed two stories;
(viii) The minimum square footage of each unit shall be 500 square feet of heated floor space;
(ix) The exterior of units shall be constructed of brick, rock, man-made rock, or cement board;
(x) The facility shall have approved septic and water systems;
(xi) The facility shall front on a COUNTY or state paved roadway;
(xii) Accessory STRUCTURES shall be for use by residents only, and may only consist of laundry BUILDINGS, water and sewer BUILDINGS, fitness centers, indoor swimming pools, park and playground BUILDINGS, and clubhouses/common use BUILDINGS. The minimum square footage of fitness centers shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of indoor swimming pool BUILDINGS shall be 1,000 square feet. The minimum square footage of park and playground BUILDINGS shall be 500 square feet. The minimum square footage of clubhouses/common use BUILDINGS shall be 1,200 square feet. Accessory STRUCTURES shall not occupy more than ten percent of total acreage;
(xiii) The facility shall have one-hour fire rated walls;
(xiv) Each unit shall have installed operational sprinklers approved and inspected by a certified third party and inspected on a routine basis to ensure proper operation;
(xv) All outdoor lighting shall be pointed in a downward direction; and
(xvi) An approved leak-proof container with close-fitting covers for the storage of garbage shall be on site. The container shall be emptied in a timely manner as to not let garbage overflow or fall onto the ground. The garbage facilities shall be adequately screened so they are not visible from the units, any STREETS, or any adjoining properties, and shall meet the setbacks of this SECTION.
(Ord. of 2-11-2013, ch. 6.06; Ord. of 2-13-2023, § 1; Ord. of 06-09-2025(1), §§ 2—4)
